# Wool occludes vibrations (VibrationSystem.Listener.isOccluded: every one of the 6 nudged lines
# from the source to the sensor crosses a block tagged occludes_vibration_signals). With the wool
# on the line, the lever's click is not heard at all; a piston whose line misses the wool still
# wakes the sensor (floor(distance) gt later). With the wool moved away (here: cleared), the same
# click wakes it 4 gt later. Use: a wool door block or wool support can make a sensor hear the
# lever on one edge only (when a moving wool block is in the way on the other), or hear a later
# door piston instead of the lever (an event-triggered window, no wire).
design designs/gadgets/sculk-wool-occlusion.txt
probe S 4 1 0
probe P 4 0 2
quiet 5
use 0 1 0
expect_trace S 0000000000
set 4 0 3 minecraft:redstone_block
expect_trace S 00++
quiet 40
clear 4 0 3
quiet 60
expect S 0
clear 2 1 0
use 0 1 0
expect_trace S 000+++
